<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martino della Torre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1263</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martino della Torre was a Milanese nobleman and leader of the popular party who in 1259 was made lord of the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, beginning the transformation of the commune into a lordship. His family, the della Torre, dominated Milan until 1277, when Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottone-visconti">Ottone Visconti</a> defeated them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-desio">Battle of Desio</a>, opening the way to Visconti rule.</p></div>
